{"Email validation calls BlockedEmail.should_block? which increments match_count and saves, causing DB writes during validation - UsersController#create runs validations at least twice (valid? then save), so a single blocked signup attempt will double-increment stats and add unnecessary DB write load": 0.9001548886299133, "BlockedEmail lookup uses exact string match, so case/whitespace variants of a blocked address can bypass blocking and allow duplicate blocked entries differing only by case - should canonicalize via Email.downcase(...).strip like other email lookups": 0.9416123628616333, "EmailValidator always queries BlockedEmail which will raise an exception if the new blocked_emails table hasn't been migrated yet during deploy - should use table_exists? guard pattern": 0.19502902030944824, "BlockedEmail.should_block? updates match_count by read-modify-write which can lose increments under concurrent requests - should be incremented atomically": 0.6500208973884583}